A note on the written content
=============================

The MIT licence above covers the software.

The handbook, school lessons, language decks and manual under `content/` are
reference material, offered in the same spirit: copy them, adapt them for
where you live, correct them, and pass them on.

They carry no warranty of any kind. Some of it concerns medicine, water
treatment, food preservation and electricity, where being wrong has
consequences. It is a starting point and a memory aid, not a substitute for
training, and not a substitute for a doctor while there is still a doctor to
be had. Verify anything that matters against another source before you rely
on it.
